//@ compile-fail
//@ error-contains: is dispatched on the type it RETURNS
//@ error-contains: nothing in hand whose tag could choose one

// The companion to `return_dispatch_onto_a_union_needs_one_impl.neon`: the same shape with
// NO impl covering the whole union, so there is nothing that can answer.
//
// `std::json` has `FromJson` for `i64` and for `str` separately. Asking for an `i64 | str`
// therefore needs a different impl per variant, chosen at run time -- and the subject is the
// return, so there is no value in hand whose tag could choose. A switch is not merely
// unhelpful here, it is unlowerable.
//
// This compiled before, and segfaulted: the switch was emitted against `args[0]`, which for
// `from_json` is the document, so a `true` fell past the `i64` test into an untested `str`
// arm and `neon_str_retain` ran on a bool payload. A compile error is the whole improvement.

use std::io;
use std::json;

fn dec(j: json::Json) throws json::JsonError -> i64 | str {
    try json::from_json(j)
}

fn main() {
    io::println(json::stringify(json::to_json(try! dec(1))));
}
